# Aarogya UI Design Rules

## Overall Visual Direction

Aarogya must look like a professionally designed Indian public service application.

The visual direction may take general inspiration from established government digital services, including the clarity and restraint of Aarogya Setu.

Do NOT copy Aarogya Setu.

Do not copy:

• Logo
• Exact screens
• Branding
• Government emblems
• Proprietary assets
• Illustrations
• Exact layouts

Aarogya must have its own visual identity.

## Design Character

The application should feel:

• Professional
• Calm
• Trustworthy
• Accessible
• Modern
• Information focused
• Appropriate for public use

It should NOT feel:

• Like a fitness startup
• Like a gaming application
• Like an AI generated dashboard
• Like a template
• Like a cryptocurrency application
• Like a social media application

## Color

Use a restrained color system.

Preferred foundation:

• White
• Light neutral surfaces
• Dark text
• Green or teal primary accent

Use warning colors intentionally:

• Amber for warnings
• Red for critical states
• Green for safe states

Do not use excessive colors.

Do not use neon colors.

Do not use gradients unless there is a strong documented reason.

## Typography

Typography must establish hierarchy.

Use:

• Clear page titles
• Strong section headings
• Readable body text
• Large values for important health metrics
• Smaller secondary metadata

Do not use excessive font weights.

Do not use decorative fonts.

## Cards

Cards should be used when they improve information grouping.

Do not put every element inside a rounded card.

Avoid:

• Giant rounded containers
• Excessive border radius
• Card inside card inside card
• Floating UI everywhere

## Spacing

Use a consistent spacing system.

Do not manually invent arbitrary spacing values for every screen.

Maintain consistent:

• Page margins
• Section spacing
• Card padding
• Button heights
• Text spacing

## Icons

Use a consistent icon library.

Icons must have a clear semantic purpose.

Do not use emojis as interface icons.

Do not mix unrelated icon styles.

## NO EMOJIS

Aarogya's application UI must contain ZERO emojis.

Do not use:

❤️
⚠️
🚨
🏥
🔥
💧
or similar emoji characters.

Use proper icons instead.

## Emergency UI

Emergency screens must prioritize information over decoration.

The user must immediately understand:

1. What happened?
2. How serious is it?
3. What should I do?
4. Is connectivity available?
5. Is emergency information being transmitted?

Critical information must be visible without scrolling whenever reasonably possible.

## Normal Mode

Normal Mode should feel calm.

Show:

• Health status
• Personal baseline
• Trends
• Relevant metrics
• Recommendations

Do not overwhelm the user with medical statistics.

## Disaster Mode

Disaster Mode should visually distinguish itself from Normal Mode.

Show:

• Disaster type
• Risk level
• Immediate action
• Location
• Connectivity
• Battery
• Relevant map or safety information

The interface should be urgent but controlled.

## Survival Mode

Survival Mode should remove unnecessary information.

Prioritize:

• Current risk
• Current relevant vitals
• Fall status
• Movement
• Location
• Battery
• Connectivity
• Emergency state

## Status Design

Never communicate critical information using color alone.

For example:

BAD:

Red background only.

GOOD:

CRITICAL
Emergency event detected
Possible fall detected

with appropriate iconography and color.

## Loading States

Every asynchronous operation needs an appropriate loading state.

Never leave a blank screen while data is loading.

## Error States

Errors must explain:

• What went wrong
• Whether the user can continue
• What action they can take

Avoid technical stack traces in the UI.

## Offline States

Offline status must be explicit.

Example:

"Internet unavailable"

"Local monitoring active"

"Emergency event stored on this device"

Do not hide offline behavior.

## Empty States

Empty states must explain what the user can do next.

Never use:

"No data."

Prefer:

"No health history available yet."

"Continue using Aarogya to establish your personal baseline."

## Animations

Use animation sparingly.

Appropriate:

• Screen transitions
• Loading indicators
• State changes
• Risk transitions

Avoid:

• Decorative floating animations
• Excessive bouncing
• Particle effects
• Animated gradients
• Unnecessary motion

The product must remain professional.

## Copywriting

Use short, factual sentences.

Good:

"Possible fall detected."

"Connectivity unavailable."

"Emergency event saved locally."

"Your current readings differ from your usual baseline."

Bad:

"Your AI guardian noticed something!"

"Don't worry, we've got you!"

"Your super intelligent AI is protecting you!"

Do not use marketing language inside the application.

## Consistency

Build reusable components.

Do not create a completely different visual system for every screen.

Every screen should look like it belongs to Aarogya.
